pa2q: KGSL builds present through the CPU (shm) WSI path.

Turnip registers its WSI as a hardware device (sw_device = false), so the
Wayland and X11 WSI build WSI_IMAGE_TYPE_DRM image params. A KGSL-only build
has no libdrm, so wsi_common.c compiles the DRM case out of get_blit_type()
and configure_image() and the release build's UNREACHABLE lets the compiler
treat every image as CPU: the DRM params' num_modifier_lists (1) is read as
the alloc_shm callback and the first vkCreateSwapchainKHR jumps to 0x1
(SIGBUS). Every Vulkan window on the desktop died that way (vkcube, zink
without kmsro, games). Report a software WSI device on KGSL instead.

--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_wsi.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_wsi.cc
@@ -38,7 +38,10 @@
 {
    VkResult result;
 
-   const struct wsi_device_options options = { .sw_device = false };
+   /* KGSL is not a DRM device: present through shm, not dma-buf images. */
+   const struct wsi_device_options options = {
+      .sw_device = strcmp(physical_device->instance->knl->name, "kgsl") == 0,
+   };
    result = wsi_device_init(&physical_device->wsi_device,
                             tu_physical_device_to_handle(physical_device),
                             tu_wsi_proc_addr,
